  "rules": "A row maps one benchmark family to one target of the dimension registry. benchmark is the family stem: with version null the row covers the stem and every id stem-<suffix> (the longest stem wins, an exact id wins over a family); with a version it covers the exact id only. metric null: every metric of the benchmark (groups still never pool metrics). type direct: the target is a registry ID and the row is coverage; proxy: the target is a registry ID and the row is never coverage (PROTO-DEC-0084 item 3); facet: the target is a facet ID; unmapped: no target. Every row is approved: its decision is PROTO-DEC-0175 item 5 or a double check, two independent checks by different families named in checks. A target is never the quarantine bucket, a crosswalk label, a removed ID or an unknown ID.",
